α»ì α«Üα»åα«»α»ìα«╡α«╛α«»α«╛α«ò!;",
    "english":  "The blazing sun has scorched the broad boulders of the wilderness,\nwhere the deer wander thirstily in search of mirage waters.\nThe dried pod of the vagai tree rattles in the hot wind\nlike the anklets of dancers in a distant hall.\nThrough such harsh wasteland my lover journeys on foot,\nbraving the arrows of highwaymen in the sun-baked pass.\nDoes he gaze upon the heat-waves and think of my tear-filled eyes,\nor has the desire for gold hardened his tender heart\nagainst the memory of our quiet embraces?",
